      "description": "Watch RB Bragantino vs Gremio highlights and goals from Brasileirão on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 23, 2026. Brazil's Serie A delivered another chapter of pure drama on August 23, 2026, as RB Bragantino hosted Gremio . Both sides took to the pitch with high ambitions, resulting in a tactically intense and physically demanding encounter. A Battle of Nerves in the Opening Period From the opening whistle, the match was characterized by a tight tactical setup where defenses consistently outperformed the attackers. Physicality was the hallmark of the first half, leading to early cautions that dictated the flow of the game. Juninho Capixaba was the first to enter the referee's book in the 25th minute. Just before the interval, in stoppage time, Erick Noriega also received a yellow card, reflecting the rising tension as both teams fought for supremacy in the middle of the park. Tactical Shifts and Player Rotations In the second half, both managers turned to their benches to find a way through the defensive lines. Gremio introduced Cristian Pavon for Tete immediately after the restart, while RB Bragantino opted for a series of changes after the hour mark, bringing on Fabinho , Henry Mosquera , and Jovane Cabral . The game remained gritty, and within a frantic four-minute window, Agustin Sant'Anna , Weverton , and Wallace were all shown yellow cards, proving that neither side was willing to concede an inch of grass. Drama in Stoppage Time As the match headed toward a stalemate, individual brilliance finally broke the deadlock. In the 86th minute, Gustavinho was introduced to provide a spark to the home side's offense. Deep into stoppage time, at the 90+5 minute mark, the breakthrough finally arrived. Gustavinho turned provider, setting up Gustavo Marques , who clinicaly found the target. It was a decisive blow that secured the points in a match defined by endurance and strategic discipline."
